/*!

@page QMMF_Recorder_Debug Debug knobs including memory dumps, key logs and properties

__Debug information prints:__

There are 3 levels of debug prints. You can set the levels with

``adb shell setprop persist.qmmf.sdk.log.level <level>``

If the level is:
+   0 : QMMF_INFO, QMMF_WARN and QMMF_ERROR will print information on the
logcat.

QMMF_INFO is used as general information print, QMMF_WARN is used for warning
prints and QMMF_ERROR handling error messages

+   1 : This level will enable the above prints plus QMMF_DEBUG print.

This prints useful information used for debugging.

+   2 : This level will enable all of the above prints plus QMMF_VERBOSE print.

This prints all possible prints.


__Proper execution for APIs:__

+   There are checks inside every API. This guarantees proper execution for
every function. If the API fails error message is printed on the logcat or
processing is stopped when necessary. Also, there are enter and exit prints to
show proper execution of an API.

__Check for failure in camera reconfiguration:__

+   Camera can be reconfigured only if camera adaptor is in idle state. Camera
adaptor goes to idle state when all capture request are processed and all
buffers are returned.

+   If the creation or destruction of streams fails that means that most likely
buffers are not returned by the Client.

__Post-processing pipe:__

+   In PostProcPipe class CreatePipe function has a print to show all nodes on
the created pipe. Below is how the print should look:

``RecorderPostProcPipe CreatePipe: Reprocess pipe: "nodes"``

+   Before stopping the pipe, Abort API is executed. This is API is blocking and
returns when all plugin ongoing processing is stopped and all buffers are
returned. Output buffer of last plugin is forward to the Client. It means that
Abort will be blocked until client returns buffer too. If the timeout is
reached, an error message will appear (like the one below) in the log.

``RecorderPostProcPipe Abort: Timed out on Wait``

__GetBuffer API debug:__

+   GetBuffer API ensures that if we've reached the maximum number of buffers,
the API will wait for free buffer. But there is a time out check. If we've
waited longer then the time out, this means that Client or Camera did not return
the buffers and buffer rotation is blocked. Also, error message will be shown in
the log:

``RecorderCamera3Stream GetBuffer: wait for output buffer return timed out``

__Frame drop:__

+   Frame drop can appear if HAL returns buffer with an error. If this happens
__CameraErrorCb__ API is called and this print is shown to the logcat:


``CameraErrorCb: Camera: *ID*, Error: *3/5*, Request: *ID*, FrameNumber: *number*``


+   Frame drop can appear if __SubmitRequest__ API fails to submit buffer.


__Frame corruption:__

+   Possible corruption of frames could come from the back-end.

+   One way to debug frame corruption is to dump and analyze the frames before
processing or before rescaler is called.

___
*/